    "## 4. Forecast demand and recommend stock\n",
    "How it works, in plain words:\n",
    "1. Demand per day is **sales plus 30% of requests** (requests are only a signal of interest).\n",
    "2. For each horizon (7, 30, 90 days) the code tests Linear Regression, Random Forest and (if installed) XGBoost on recent history it did not train on.\n",
    "3. A model is used only if it beats a simple baseline (\"the recent daily rate continues\") by at least 5%.\n",
    "4. Reorder quantity covers the supplier lead time plus a 30-day review period, with a safety margin, minus the stock held."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "result = forecast_products(requests, sales, stock)\n",
    "forecasts = result[\"forecasts\"]\n",
    "forecasts.drop(columns=[\"notes\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.1 Which model was used?\n",
    "Mean absolute error (MAE) on the hold-out period. Lower is better. If no model beats `naive_rate` by enough, the baseline is used."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = []\n",
